{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree\/reingoldTilfordLayout()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()","externalID":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV12GraphDrawingE21reingoldTilfordLayoutAD0E0VyxGyF","modules":[{"relatedModules":["Trees"],"name":"GraphDrawing"}],"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"Trees","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift#L34"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The root is at (0, 0) and a vertex at depth d has y = d. Children are placed left to right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, vertices at one depth at least 1 apart along each subtree’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contour, and every parent centred over its first and last child. Where two subtrees had to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be pushed apart, the smaller subtrees between them are spaced evenly (Walker’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"improvement), so a mirrored tree draws as the reflection of the drawing and isomorphic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subtrees are drawn identically up to translation. Coordinates are multiples of a power of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"½, exact in "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reingold and Tilford, “Tidier drawings of trees”, IEEE Transactions on Software"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Engineering SE-7(2), 1981."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Walker, “A node-positioning algorithm for general trees”, Software: Practice and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Experience 20(7), 1990.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert, “Improving Walker’s algorithm to run in linear time”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Graph Drawing (GD 2002), LNCS 2528, 2002.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n) time and memory, with no recursion.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","doc:\/\/Gra